# Components (Astro)

**Scope:** `apps/website`, `packages/ui`, `packages/devtools` — `.astro` files.

**Rule index:** `.cursor/rules/README.md`.

Works with **`website-architecture.mdc`** and **`website-behaviour.mdc`**.

---

## packages/ui vs apps/website

- **`packages/ui`** — Core UI: Header, Footer, buttons, hero, dialogs, etc. Grouped by domain folders. **No** app logic, **no** CMS, **no** `@rotate/cms`. May contain **approved** client JS per **When to use JS** below.
- **`apps/website`** — Layout, **`*-container`** folders, and thin **wrappers** only. Containers fetch and pass props to `packages/ui`. Layout (`base-layout.astro`) binds design-system + devtools.

**Rule:** Website `src/components/` holds **`*-container`** (and optional wrappers). **Do not** grow ad-hoc “smart” components in website that duplicate `packages/ui`.

---

## Folder grouping: container, wrapper, core

| Kind | Folder / file | Data? | Client JS? |
|------|----------------|-------|------------|
| **Container** | `components/<name>-container/index.astro` + optional `format-<name>.ts` | Yes — `@rotate/cms` getters | **No** |
| **Wrapper** | Optional `components/<name>/` or shared shell in `packages/ui` | **No** | Only if the wrapped **core** component requires it |
| **Core** | `packages/ui/src/<domain>/…` | **No** | Only per escalation (`website-behaviour.mdc`) |

**Example:**

```text
apps/website/src/components/
  hero-container/
    index.astro     ← server: getters + format → props
    format-hero.ts  ← pure CMS shape → UI props (optional)

packages/ui/src/hero/
  hero.astro
  hero-wrapper.astro     ← optional: `<script src="./hero-client.ts">` (one module load; listeners attach at module evaluation)
  hero-client.ts         ← client lifecycle: init, visibility, intersection, word cycling
```

**Comments on `format-*.ts` and colocated `*.ts`:** Follow **`functional-style.mdc` — Comments** (minimal inline; JSDoc on functions that encode non-obvious or heavy logic).

---

## When to use JavaScript

1. **Default:** **No** client JS. Server HTML + CSS (`design-system.mdc`: `tablet:` / `desktop:`, tokens).
2. **Need per-request HTML?** Server Island — **`website-behaviour.mdc`** (comment why).
3. **Need toggle / scroll / focus only?** Minimal JS in **`packages/ui`** (or native `<details>` / `<dialog>` first).
4. **Need multi-step client UI state?** Alpine **last**, only in core components — **`website-behaviour.mdc`**.

**Forbidden:** Client `<script>` in **`*-container/index.astro`** for interactivity — move behaviour into `packages/ui` or use CSS/native elements.

---

## How to add JavaScript (core components)

When a **core** component needs TypeScript on the client:

- **Folder:** Component lives in its own folder under `packages/ui/src/…`
- **Files:** `name.astro` + colocated **`name.ts`**
- **Shared helpers:** `@rotate/utilities` — workspace package; group UI-facing helpers under `src/ui/` (e.g. `prefers-reduced-motion.ts`) and re-export from `src/ui/index.ts`. Import **`@rotate/utilities/ui`** (barrel). Keep browser/SSR-safe (`typeof window`) where relevant.
- **Wire-up:** `<script src="./name.ts" />` in the `.astro` file — **no** large inline scripts. Prefer **one** `src` entry so the client module is not pulled in as separate inline chunks; bootstrapping (listeners, etc.) can live at the end of that module — it runs once per module evaluation (see `hero-client.ts`).
- **Progressive enhancement:** Markup must stay usable if JS fails

```
packages/ui/src/dialog/
  dialog.astro
  dialog.ts
```

```astro
<div data-dialog>...</div>
<script src="./dialog.ts" />
```

Islands / `client:*` directives: use **only** with the same justification as other client JS, and prefer keeping logic in colocated modules.

